[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `B->A`
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `B->D`
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m This means:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `B` is an upstream cause of `A` and `D`
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `A` and `D` are descendants of `B`
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m So, if `B` is perturbed, then:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `B` is 0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `A` and `D` are 1
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - `C` is not reachable from `B`, so it is 0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m Thus, the effect of perturbing `B` would be:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m ```
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m Perturb(B) -> B:0 A:1 D:1
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m ```
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
