[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m This creates a directed path from A to D, with no other edges. So:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - A is an ancestor of C and D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - C is an ancestor of D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - D is a descendant of A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m So, if A is perturbed, then:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - A: 0 (perturbed)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - C: 1 (descendant of A)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - D: 1 (descendant of C)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m So the expected values for perturbing A would be:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m ```
