[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m ### **Perturbation: B -> A:1, B:0, C:1, D:1**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m We check if B is an upstream cause of A, C, and D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - **B->C** and **B->D** are present in the graph.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - **C->A** is also present.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - So, B → C → A, and B → D → A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m Thus, **A, C, D** are descendants of B.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m So, perturbing B would set B to 0 and make A, C, D to 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m Which matches:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m **Perturb(B) -> A:1, B:0, C:1, D:1** ✅
