[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - A is perturbed → A:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - A → C → C:1
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - So C is a downstream of A
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - B: A → B is not a descendant of A. So B:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - D: A → D is not a descendant of A. So D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m Thus, the result is A:0, B:0, C:1, D:0 → matches the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m ✅ So this case is consistent.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m #### **Case 2: Perturb(B)**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - B is perturbed → B:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - B → A → C → D → C
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m So:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - A is a descendant of B
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - C is a descendant of B
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - D is a descendant of B
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - So the downstream descendants of B are A, C, D
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m So the result would be:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m - A:1, B:0, C:1, D:1 → which matches the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3660498)[0m 
